<title>USA: Litton wins orders for two more Navy ships.</title>
<headline>Litton wins orders for two more Navy ships.</headline>
<dateline>WOODLAND HILLS, Calif 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Litton Industries Inc on Friday said the U.S. Navy exercised a $659.4 million contract option to order two additional guided missile destroyers from its Ingalls Shipbuilding division.</p>
<p>The shipyard has received contracts to build 17 DDG 51 Class Aegis destroyers since 1987. Nine of the ships have been delivered.</p>
<p>The award brings Ingalls' business backlog to about $3.8 billion, involving construction of 11 U.S. Navy surface warships.</p>
</text>
